.TH LIBMPQ__FILE_NUMBER_FROM_HASH 3 2026-08-14 "The MoPaQ archive library"
.SH NAME
libmpq__file_number_from_hash \- resolve an MPQ filename hash to its file number.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <libmpq/mpq.h>
.sp
.BI "int32_t libmpq__file_number_from_hash("
.BI "        mpq_archive_s *" "mpq_archive,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "hash1,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "hash2,"
.BI "        uint32_t " "hash3,"
.BI "        uint32_t *" "number"
.BI ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
Resolve precomputed Storm filename hashes using only the classic MPQ hash
table. Supply all three values from
.BR libmpq__file_hash (3)
for the same filename. \fIhash1\fP selects the initial probe slot,
and \fIhash2\fP and \fIhash3\fP match the stored hash pair.
.PP
HET/BET lookup requires the filename to compute a separate hash. Members
reachable only through HET/BET are unavailable through this function,
including in mixed archives. In a mixed archive a classic hit can resolve
to the same canonical file number as an HET/BET hit, or select a different
member under classic first-hit rules. When the filename is available, use
.BR libmpq__file_number (3)
for ordinary lookup or
.BR libmpq__file_number_from_identity (3)
for an exact locale/platform tuple.
.LP
The first argument is an archive handle opened by
\fBlibmpq__archive_open\fP(). The function stores the matching file number
in \fInumber\fP.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, zero is returned and the file number is stored in \fInumber\fP.
On error, one of the following constants is returned.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_EXIST
A required archive or output pointer is NULL, the archive has no classic
hash table, or no live classic slot matches the supplied hashes. These
cases leave any supplied output untouched.
.TP
.B LIBMPQ_ERROR_FORMAT
A matching classic slot does not resolve to a valid canonical file entry.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR libmpq (3),
.BR libmpq__file_hash (3),
.BR libmpq__file_number (3),
.BR libmpq__file_number_from_identity (3)
